% SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
% =====================================================================
% queries.clausal -- QUERY-COMBINATOR layer for eu/dora_rts_review_report_format.
% A TOP-LAYER consumer: it imports the determination slice's PUBLIC
% predicates it calls, and nothing else (plus implements/1 for markers).
%
% dora_rts_review_report_format_profile_keys/1: the thirty-six profile keys, in
%     root_exports / input_contract order.
% dora_rts_review_report_format_input_problems/2: THE INPUT CHECK, re-exported
%     from the kernel as the scaffold wrote it ([] = none).
% dora_rts_review_report_format_what_if/4 (#16 what-if): set one key of the
%     attribute list to a hypothetical value and re-evaluate the completeness
%     status (Art 27(1) and (2) of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU)
%     2024/1774). The kit override_key/4 works on dicts, and this order types
%     the profile as an attribute list, so the override is local plumbing.
% dora_rts_review_report_format_compliance_check/3 (#13 compliance_check):
%     is the proposed action submit_review_report, with the report as it
%     stands, compliant with Article 27? compliant for complete,
%     non_compliant for incomplete; every other answer of the completeness
%     query (the gate, the request, a status compound) passes through as is.
%     The deny-overrides lattice of kit/compliance_lib adds nothing to one
%     action checked against one content rule (NOTES.md).
% Eligibility (#2) and justification (#7) are served by the slice's
% verdict and its cited checklist (one cite(...) per item), through the
% package facade.
%
% RESULT CONSTRUCTORS AND ROOT ATOMS. The order's root_exports (the
% thirty-six profile keys, the five result atoms, the twenty-nine duty
% atoms and the judgement value unsure) are read as package-root module
% attributes, and the result constructors are exported: each is defined
% here by one clause and is never called as a query (unknown_key/1 is
% pure data and has no clause). They decide nothing statutory, so they
% carry no implements/1 marker.
% =====================================================================

:- module(queries, [
    dora_rts_review_report_format_profile_keys/1,
    dora_rts_review_report_format_input_problems/2,
    dora_rts_review_report_format_what_if/4,
    dora_rts_review_report_format_compliance_check/3,
    complete/0,
    incomplete/0,
    none_outstanding/0,
    simplified_framework_entity/0,
    framework_review_report_not_requested/0,
    unsure/0,
    required/1,
